# jwks-server environment variables
# DO NOT commit real key material.
#
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# REQUIRED: ADMIN_JWKS_B64  (base64-encoded JWKS JSON)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# This is the ONLY supported configuration method.
# ADMIN_JWKS_PAYLOAD is no longer supported and will cause a hard FATAL.
#
# Why base64?
#   Passing raw JSON via Railway CLI / PowerShell corrupts the value:
#   {"keys":[...]} becomes {keys:[...]} which is not valid JSON.
#   Base64 is plain alphanumeric — safe in any shell without quoting.
#
# How to generate + set (run locally, NEVER commit jwks.json output):
#
#   PowerShell (from directory containing jwks.json):
#     $b64 = [Convert]::ToBase64String([Text.Encoding]::UTF8.GetBytes((Get-Content -Raw .\jwks.json)))
#     Write-Host $b64
#
#   Bash:
#     base64 -w0 jwks.json
#
#   Set in Railway (no quoting issues):
#     railway variables set "ADMIN_JWKS_B64=<the-base64-string>" --service jwks-server
#
#   Delete old broken variable if present:
#     railway variables delete ADMIN_JWKS_PAYLOAD --service jwks-server
#
# ADMIN_JWKS_B64=<base64-encoded-jwks-json>

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ⛔ DEPRECATED — DO NOT USE
# ADMIN_JWKS_PAYLOAD is REMOVED. Setting it will crash the server
# with a FATAL error and exact remediation instructions.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# PORT — Railway sets this automatically
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
PORT=3001
